WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.775
The best proof a linter is useful
is that it finds something real.

2
00:00:03.775 --> 00:00:06.931
Run against the HR-Driven
Identity book's own

3
00:00:06.931 --> 00:00:10.087
table of rule patterns,
it found three things.

4
00:00:10.087 --> 00:00:13.564
One pattern had no guest guard,
so a guest with a matching

5
00:00:13.564 --> 00:00:16.813
employer name could have
qualified; that's now fixed.

6
00:00:16.813 --> 00:00:19.303
Another let in a worker
with an empty type,

7
00:00:19.303 --> 00:00:23.112
and the owner decided that shouldn't
count, so it gained a clause.

8
00:00:23.112 --> 00:00:26.249
And the direct reports rule
can't carry guards at all,

9
00:00:26.249 --> 00:00:31.130
because Learn says it can't be combined
with anything, so the linter just notes it.
